1
00:00:01,128 --> 00:00:02,303
You're late.

2
00:00:03,053 --> 00:00:06,631
Traffic on the bridge.
There was an accident.

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:11,992
There's always an accident with you.

4
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:14,622
Did you bring it?

5
00:00:15,154 --> 00:00:16,600
It's in the car.

6
00:00:19,052 --> 00:00:21,919
Then why are we standing here?

7
00:00:22,993 --> 00:00:26,679
Because I want to know what I'm carrying first.

8
00:00:27,897 --> 00:00:31,005
You don't want to know. Trust me.

9
00:00:31,354 --> 00:00:35,040
Trust is exactly what I'm running low on.

10
00:00:35,605 --> 00:00:37,361
Fine.
Open the trunk.

11
00:00:38,024 --> 00:00:40,888
Not here. Too many windows.

12
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,592
Nobody's watching us, Daniel.

13
00:00:44,102 --> 00:00:46,596
Somebody's always watching.

14
00:00:49,652 --> 00:00:51,901
You sound like your father.

15
00:00:52,197 --> 00:00:54,631
Leave him out of this.

16
00:00:54,773 --> 00:00:58,003
He's the reason we're both here.

17
00:00:58,186 --> 00:01:01,546
He's the reason you have a job.

18
00:01:01,948 --> 00:01:03,664
Was. Past tense.

19
00:01:04,797 --> 00:01:06,253
...

20
00:01:07,344 --> 00:01:10,290
Just drive. I'll explain on the way.

21
00:01:10,836 --> 00:01:13,396
Explain now, or I walk.

22
00:01:13,664 --> 00:01:16,895
You walk, and they'll find you by morning.

23
00:01:18,282 --> 00:01:19,868
Is that a threat?

24
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:22,953
It's the weather forecast.

25
00:01:23,619 --> 00:01:25,348
Get in the car.

26
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:28,167
If anything happens to me—

27
00:01:29,366 --> 00:01:32,112
Nothing's going to happen.

28
00:01:36,212 --> 00:01:40,270
If anything happens,
the envelope goes to the police.

29
00:01:40,515 --> 00:01:42,365
There's no envelope.

30
00:01:42,623 --> 00:01:45,720
There's always an envelope.
